From 441512b99db16110522ef055ffbb4d18226ea115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jetha Chan <jethachan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:57:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] glsl: implement EXT_shader_16bit_storage

EXT_shader_16bit_storage adds float16_t, int16_t, uint16_t and their
2- to 4-component vectors for uniform and buffer storage.  Values can be
loaded, stored to buffers and converted to and from the 32-bit types
with constructors; other uses are not allowed.

- Enable the float16 scalar and vector type names (already there for
  AMD_gpu_shader_half_float) and add the int16 and uint16 ones.
- Add constructor conversions between int16_t/uint16_t and int/uint, and
  reject 16-bit constructor conversions the extension does not allow
  (AMD_gpu_shader_half_float keeps allowing any float16 conversion).
- Reject variable declarations outside uniform and buffer blocks, and
  arithmetic and relational operators, on these types unless
  AMD_gpu_shader_half_float makes float16_t a full type.

Buffer layout and lowering to 16-bit load/store intrinsics already work
for 16-bit types.

Not enforced yet: the rules against swizzles and vector array
subscripting of 16-bit vectors, and default-block uniforms of structure
type with 16-bit members are rejected rather than allowed.
